CONFUSION MATRIX- 
The confusion matrix is another way to evaluate the performance of a classifier. Here, it counts the number of times
instances of class A are classified as class B. For example, the number of times the classifier confused images of 5s 
with non-5s.The confusion matrix is a matrix with four different combinations of predicted and actual classes: 
True Positive (TP), True Negative (TN), False Positive (FP), and False Negative (FN).

