ROC curve- 
he ROC curve is drawn by calculating the true positive rate (TPR) and false positive rate (FPR) at every possible
threshold (in practice, at selected intervals), then graphing TPR over FPR.
Y axis- TPR (sensitivity)
X axis- FPR ( specificity)
threshold is the point where the curve starts flatlining.
The ROC curve plots the true positive rate against the false positive rate at various thresholds.

AUC Curve- its used for multiple models 
Multple ROC curves are ploted and to pick the ROC curve which covers the most area will be the best model.

AUC-ROC measures the area 
under this curve which provides an aggregate measure of a model's performance across different classification thresholds.

         
